Triangle \(ABC\)

a) is circumscribed around a circle of radius 1;
b)* is inscribed in a circle of radius 1;

The radii of the triangle's excircles are denoted as \(r_{a}, r_{b},\) and \(r_{c}\), where \(r_{a} \leq r_{b} \leq r_{c}\). What values can the following take:

1) the radius \(r_{a}\) of the excircle;
2) the radius \(r_{b}\);
3) the radius \(r_{c}\)?

Can a regular tetrahedron with an edge length of 1 pass through a circular hole with a radius of:
a) 0.45;
b) 0.44? (The thickness of the hole can be neglected.)
